# Avalanche Framework - Quick Start Guide

Get started with remote command control, pentesting, and reporting in minutes.

---

## Installation

1. **Copy all modules to your project:**
   ```
   CommandServer.js
   PentestModule.js
   ReportingEngine.js
   PayloadTemplates.js
   Integration.js
   ```

2. **Import in your HTML/JS:**
   ```html
   <script type="module">
     import AvalancheFramework from './Integration.js';
     window.avalanche = new AvalancheFramework();
     await window.avalanche.initialize();
   </script>
   ```

---

## 30-Second Setup

```javascript
// Create instance
const avalanche = new AvalancheFramework({
  commandServerUrl: 'ws://your-c2-server:8080'
});

// Initialize
await avalanche.initialize();

// Run scan
const results = await avalanche.runSecurityAssessment();

// Export report
avalanche.exportReport('html');
```

---

## Common Tasks

### 1. Run Security Scan

```javascript
const results = await avalanche.runSecurityAssessment();

console.log(`Total issues: ${results.summary.totalIssues}`);
console.log(`Critical: ${results.summary.criticalIssues}`);
console.log(`High: ${results.summary.highIssues}`);
```

### 2. Get Specific Findings

```javascript
// XSS issues only
const xssIssues = avalanche.getResults('xss');

// CSRF issues only
const csrfIssues = avalanche.getResults('csrf');

// Auth issues only
const authIssues = avalanche.getResults('auth');
```

